   "steps": [
    [
     "Oven",
     "Preheat the oven to 200°C (400°F) and grease or line a large baking tray."
    ],
    [
     "Mix",
     "Mix the chicken mince with the seasonings, harissa and olive oil for 2–3 minutes until slightly sticky, so it binds without eggs or breadcrumbs."
    ],
    [
     "Spread",
     "Flatten evenly on the tray, about 2 cm thick."
    ],
    [
     "Shape",
     "Cut into equal strips with a knife, then press your fingers along each strip to make kebab ridges."
    ],
    [
     "Bake",
     "Bake near the top of the oven 20–25 minutes until lightly golden and cooked through (75°C inside). Don't overcook so they stay juicy."
    ],
    [
     "Finish",
     "Mix the harissa and olive oil with the pan juices, brush over the kebabs and garnish with parsley."
    ]
   ],
   "notes": "Recipe is the creator's, from her comment on the post; it serves 5–6. She gives no macros, so they're my estimate for 5 servings with thigh mince (breast mince would be leaner).",
